#! program build/docs-examples/bin/tut12_run
#! fresh   /tmp/figure-studio
#! args    --examples /tmp/figure-studio --case /tmp/figure-studio/plate
#! frames  330
#! poster  300
# --check on macOS: FIGURE's title bar has its buttons on the left there, the menus after them (by design): the bar
# masked, the rest compared (run 43649582637, 2026-11-14)
#! mask.darwin 0 0 1100 22
# and the residuals' plot: 27 pixel(s) over 2 there (Apple's libm), 64 allowed
#! check.darwin max_failed=64
# --check on Windows: the residuals' plot, 27 pixel(s) over 2 as on macOS (the C library's maths, not glibc's;
# run 43744364220, 2026-11-15): 64 allowed
#! check.win32 max_failed=64
# Run: the solver's lines fill the log, the residual plot grows on a logarithmic axis, the status bar shows the
# iteration and the progress towards the tolerance; at the end a notification says the solver converged
# (the solver runs in real time while the frames are drawn at the capture's pace: the video's timing depends on the
# machine, the poster is the end of the run)
0   move 600 300
10  move 384 384 15
30  down
32  up
50  move 700 250 30
200 wait
